WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Today, I learned that vitamins were discovered&nbsp;
by the butter industry. It's like 1913,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.680
and the margarine industry is threatening to&nbsp;
compete with butter. Margarine being a fat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.460
substitute that's not made from dairy. Anyway. So&nbsp;
these massive dairy industries like in Wisconsin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.780
are like, “No way, Jose. Butter is better&nbsp;
than margarine. We got to prove it.” So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.860
they do what corporations have always done&nbsp;
and continue to do, which is hire scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.700
to prove that their product is actually really&nbsp;
good. And soon they're showing that the rats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.240
that ate butter were like better than the&nbsp;
ones that ate margarine And they were like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.040
“Oh, this is like a good marketing thing. But&nbsp;
like, why are the butter-fed rats fatter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.360
happier and healthier?” And in doing all their&nbsp;
experiments, they isolated this micronutrient,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.860
this molecule that our bodies need. They called it&nbsp;
a vitamin. And because the one that they found in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.100
butter was like the first one they discovered,&nbsp;
they're like, “what should we call it?” “A,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.320
like first letter of the alphabet, Vitamin A.”&nbsp;
That's how we got vitamin A. Since then, we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:58.080
discovered 13 essential vitamins. So you can thank&nbsp;
butter for vitamins. Thank you, butter. Love you.

